Sval: a restored tab validates its page with the server

SessionStore restores a tab's page through nsSHistory::ReloadCurrentEntry,
which loads it as a history load. nsDocShellLoadState::CalculateChannelLoadFlags
gives a history load VALIDATE_NEVER, so a tab brought back with the session
shows the copy the cache kept from the last one, however old, until the user
reloads it. Loading it as a reload asks the server whether the page changed,
as reloading the tab does. Session store keeps no POST data, so the reload's
resend prompt cannot show.

diff --git a/docshell/shistory/nsSHistory.cpp b/docshell/shistory/nsSHistory.cpp
index 1a7c5580b8..6c465a8ffb 100644
--- a/docshell/shistory/nsSHistory.cpp
+++ b/docshell/shistory/nsSHistory.cpp
@@ -1806,8 +1806,10 @@ nsresult nsSHistory::ReloadCurrentEntry(
   // Notify listeners
   NotifyListeners(mListeners, [](auto l) { l->OnHistoryGotoIndex(); });
 
-  return LoadEntry(/* aSourceBrowsingContext */ nullptr, mIndex, LOAD_HISTORY,
-                   HIST_CMD_RELOAD, aLoadResults,
+  // A reload's load type, so the restored page is validated with the server.
+  // A history load takes a cached copy without asking.
+  return LoadEntry(/* aSourceBrowsingContext */ nullptr, mIndex,
+                   LOAD_RELOAD_NORMAL, HIST_CMD_RELOAD, aLoadResults,
                    /* aSameEpoch */ false, /* aLoadCurrentEntry */ true,
                    /* aUserActivation */ false);
 }
